	)
	(text_box "Sequencing: the ECP5 has no order requirement (VCCIO before or with VCC is recommended, and 3.3 V comes up first here because the 1.1 V buck's input capacitor charges through the same 5 V). The PHY, converters and amplifiers all tolerate any\norder."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 317.5 0)
		(size 180.34 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "838018ef-d623-e235-f6fb-638349c5f11d")
	)
	(text_box "Everything runs from the 5 V of the FTDI USB-C (or a bench 5 V on J16, diode-OR'd). The two switching regulators make the digital 3.3 V (FPGA I/O, SDRAM, flash, PHY, FTDI) and the 1.1 V core; they are placed in the far corner from the converters. Every analog rail is a separate LDO off the 5 V: +3V3_ADC (AD9238 and its drivers), +3V3_DAC (AD9767); the op amps get +5VA through a ferrite and\n-4.5 V from an LM27761 charge pump. The converters' digital supplies and the PHY are fed from +3V3 through ferrite beads so their switching noise does not ride the common rail. Budget: FPGA ~0.6 W, ADC 0.6 W, DAC 0.4 W, PHY 0.4 W, FTDI 0.3 W, amplifiers 0.4 W, SDRAM 0.2 W: about 3 W, 0.6 A at 5 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(size 340.36 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "85e2c336-a3ee-c4bc-b9b0-ddca7e7e9611")
	)
